<title>UK: TABLE - BG Q1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - BG Q1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.5		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Pretax		     615		    vs 560</p>
<p> Profit after tax	 418		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Turnover		   1,435		  vs 1,354</p>
<p>NOTE - All figures are on a historical cost basis. BG said it was impossible to give a 1996 tax charge because of the British Gas demerger in February 1997. There are therefore no comparative after tax figures.</p>
<p>Full company name - BG Plc, which is the renamed rump of British Gas after this company spun off its domestic gas supply business and Centrica Plc was formed through a demerger in February.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
